# Project CHAOS - Python backend overrides
#
# Written once by the installer. NEVER overwritten by an upgrade and NEVER
# removed by an uninstall.
#
# Every setting in src/chaos/config.py (class Settings) is listed below as
# CHAOS_<FIELD>, commented out, with the platform's own default. The gateway
# (the ChaosHost service) reads this file at startup and hands every
# uncommented line to the Python backend, to first-run setup, and to the
# nightly backup and retention pass. It does not rely on machine environment
# variables, because the Service Control Manager hands a service the
# environment block it inherited at boot and an installer cannot change that
# for a service starting in the same session.
#
# Grammar: KEY=VALUE, one per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored, an
# optional "export " prefix is tolerated, surrounding quotes are stripped, and
# there is no variable expansion and no escaping. A line with no "=" is
# reported on GET /host/info (installation.backendEnvironmentProblems), not
# guessed at. The gateway reports the NAMES of the variables it read from this
# file and never the values, because this file may hold credentials.
#
# What you cannot usefully change here, because the gateway sets it on every
# launch:
#
#   CHAOS_SUPERVISOR_STOP_SECRET
#       Generated by the gateway for every launch of the backend and used to
#       ask it to stop cleanly over loopback. Never set it here: a value here
#       is overridden, and could only make the stop request fail.
#   the listen address
#       The gateway launches `chaos serve --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8081` (from
#       Chaos:BackendUrl in chaos.host.json), so CHAOS_API_HOST and
#       CHAOS_API_PORT below do not apply to the supervised backend. Loopback
#       only, on purpose: the gateway is the only LAN listener.
#   PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1, PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
#       So the backend's log lines arrive on time, in UTF-8, without .pyc
#       writes into the install directory.
#
# CHAOS_DATABASE_URL and CHAOS_DATA_DIR are resolved once by the gateway from
# chaos.host.json, this file and the installed layout (in that order of
# preference), and the one answer goes to the backend, to first-run setup and
# to the nightly backup alike; GET /host/info (storage.databaseUrlSource,
# storage.dataDirectorySource) names the source that won. A value here is
# honoured.
#
# The installer also sets machine-wide variables for a human at a prompt and
# for chaos.cmd (CHAOS_HOME, CHAOS_DATA, CHAOS_PYTHON, CHAOS_WEB_ROOT,
# CHAOS_DATA_DIR, CHAOS_SCHEMA_DIR, CHAOS_API_HOST). The service may not see
# those until the next boot, which is the reason this file exists.
#
# Uncomment a line and restart the service to change it:
#   Restart-Service ChaosHost   (elevated), or services.msc.

# --- Identity ---------------------------------------------------------------
# primary | secondary. A secondary control node observes and alerts and
# deliberately cannot issue commands (SDD 16.1); with the bus enabled it runs
# no command dispatch. If this node is the one in a separate structure, set it
# here and confirm with:  chaos.cmd status
#CHAOS_NODE_ROLE=primary
#CHAOS_SITE_ID=site.site.primary.01
# IANA zone name. The platform stamps and schedules in it; the gateway's own
# nightly backup runs on the machine's Windows time zone, not this one.
#CHAOS_TIMEZONE=America/Toronto

# --- Storage ----------------------------------------------------------------
# A SQLAlchemy URL, not a path: forward slashes, even on Windows. The installed
# default, used when this is commented out and chaos.host.json names nothing,
# is the file below; chaos.cmd uses the same file, so the service and the
# command line never end up with two databases. PostgreSQL needs the
# "postgres" extra in the embedded runtime; rebuild it with
#   .\build.ps1 -Task runtime -IncludePostgres
#CHAOS_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///C:/ProgramData/Project CHAOS/db/homestead.db
# Log every SQL statement. Diagnostic only; it makes the log enormous.
#CHAOS_SQL_ECHO=false

# --- Machine-readable design package ----------------------------------------
# The registry is built from data\ and validated against schemas\. The
# installed defaults are the copies the installer lays down; `chaos validate`
# and `chaos load-all` work from them with no repository checkout.
#CHAOS_DATA_DIR=C:\Program Files\Project CHAOS\app\data
# The gateway does not set this one. The installer sets it machine-wide, which
# the service may not see until the next boot, and the platform's own default
# (a schemas\ folder beside its package) does not exist in the embedded
# runtime. Set it here if `chaos validate` or the backup's design-package copy
# reports missing schemas.
#CHAOS_SCHEMA_DIR=C:\Program Files\Project CHAOS\app\schemas

# --- MQTT -------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PLATFORM'S OWN DEFAULT IS true. An installed node therefore starts its
# bus client against 127.0.0.1:1883 straight away; with no broker there, the
# client keeps retrying in the background and the API still comes up, but
# nothing flows on the bus and the log says so on every attempt.
#
# Set false to run the API with no bus: the bus-driven services (telemetry
# ingest, command dispatch) are then not started at all. Leave it false until
# a broker exists and per-device credentials have been issued
# (deploy/mosquitto/README.md); one shared secret turns a compromised
# greenhouse sensor into broker-wide command authority.
#CHAOS_MQTT_ENABLED=true
#CHAOS_MQTT_HOST=127.0.0.1
#CHAOS_MQTT_PORT=1883
# Credentials are per device and per node (SDD 15.2). Blank means none.
#CHAOS_MQTT_USERNAME=
#CHAOS_MQTT_PASSWORD=
#CHAOS_MQTT_CLIENT_ID=chaos-core
#CHAOS_MQTT_BASE_TOPIC=chaos
# TLS to the broker (deploy/mosquitto/README.md, "Enabling TLS"). The CA
# bundle is what makes a private-CA broker verifiable at all: without it the
# system trust store is used, which cannot verify one, and the platform warns.
# The client certificate and key are for the later step where the broker
# requires one (require_certificate true). Paths, forward or back slashes.
#CHAOS_MQTT_TLS=false
#CHAOS_MQTT_TLS_CA=
#CHAOS_MQTT_TLS_CERT=
#CHAOS_MQTT_TLS_KEY=
# Skips hostname verification of the broker certificate. Never the default: a
# broker that cannot be verified must not carry command traffic. For a bench
# where the certificate's name cannot match, and logged as the weakening it is.
#CHAOS_MQTT_TLS_INSECURE=false

# --- Historian --------------------------------------------------------------
# sql writes samples to the relational historian table; it is the shipped
# backend and the only one the product ships.
#CHAOS_HISTORIAN_BACKEND=sql
# How long raw samples are kept (SDD 16.4). Alarm and command audit records are
# kept indefinitely. The gateway's nightly retention pass reports what this
# would delete and, only with Retention.Apply true in chaos.host.json, deletes it.
#CHAOS_HISTORIAN_RAW_RETENTION_DAYS=90

# --- Backups and platform availability --------------------------------------
# Where `chaos backup` writes and where the backup-age monitor looks for the
# newest archive (it publishes backup_age_h, which the shipped backup_overdue
# alarm watches). Leave it unset: the gateway hands the backend the folder its
# own nightly backup writes to (Chaos:Backup:Directory in chaos.host.json,
# %ProgramData%\Project CHAOS\backups by default), so the two agree. A value
# here wins over the gateway's, and then the nightly archive and the monitor
# can disagree about which folder is "the" backup folder.
#CHAOS_BACKUP_DIRECTORY=
# The asset whose backup_age_h point the monitor publishes.
#CHAOS_BACKUP_AGE_ASSET_ID=it.application_service.rack_01.postgres_01
# The registry asset that stands for this platform instance. With MQTT on, the
# backend registers a retained "offline" last will on that asset's availability
# topic and publishes "online" on connect, which is what lets the class-scoped
# service_unavailable alarm fire for the API itself. Unset: the primary's
# shipped asset (it.application_service.rack_01.digital_twin_api_01); nothing
# on a secondary.
#CHAOS_PLATFORM_ASSET_ID=

# --- Telemetry semantics ----------------------------------------------------
# A point with no sample for this long reads as stale, unless its definition
# says otherwise.
#CHAOS_DEFAULT_STALE_AFTER_S=60

# --- API --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host and port are fixed by the gateway's command line for the supervised
# backend (see the top of this file); these apply only to a backend started by
# hand with `chaos serve` and no --host/--port.
#CHAOS_API_HOST=127.0.0.1
#CHAOS_API_PORT=8081
#CHAOS_API_TITLE=Project CHAOS API
# Prefix when the API is served below a path. The gateway proxies it at the
# root, so leave it empty here.
#CHAOS_API_ROOT_PATH=

# --- Overview thresholds ----------------------------------------------------
# The property overview derives a freeze or heat risk from the site's outside
# air temperature. Commissioning values, not agronomic decisions; move them
# for this site rather than editing code.
#CHAOS_OVERVIEW_FREEZE_RISK_C=2.0
#CHAOS_OVERVIEW_HEAT_RISK_C=32.0

# --- The safety gate --------------------------------------------------------
# THE global master switch for physical control. It defaults to false and it
# should stay false until the subsystem you intend to control has passed all
# twelve steps of the SDD section 19 commissioning sequence and has the records
# to show for it. Enabling it does not arm anything that has not been
# commissioned -- per-binding gates still apply -- but it is the switch that
# makes the platform capable of moving plant. See docs/commissioning.md.
#CHAOS_ALLOW_PHYSICAL_CONTROL=false
# How long a supervisory command stays valid when the request names no TTL.
#CHAOS_COMMAND_DEFAULT_TTL_S=300

# --- EMS --------------------------------------------------------------------
#CHAOS_EMS_ENABLED=true
#CHAOS_EMS_TICK_INTERVAL_S=5

# --- Alarms and notification ------------------------------------------------
#CHAOS_ALARM_ENGINE_ENABLED=true
# Comma-separated channels this node has enabled: log, email, push, voice.
#   log    always present, whatever is listed: the gateway log is never silent.
#   email  implemented: an SMTP relay, configured below.
#   push   implemented: a self-hosted, ntfy-compatible HTTP endpoint, below.
#   voice  an honest stub. CUCM is a planned functional position; selecting it
#          records "not configured" on every attempt and sends nothing.
# Severity decides which channels an alarm tries (info and warning: log;
# major: log and email; critical: log, email and push; emergency: all four),
# unless the alarm definition's escalation path says otherwise. A channel the
# path names but this list does not enable is still RECORDED as not
# configured, so "we paged you" never quietly becomes "nobody was paged".
#CHAOS_NOTIFICATION_BACKENDS=log
# Who to tell, per role, one grammar for both lines:
#   role=addr,addr;role=addr      roles: operator, on_call, maintainer
# Email addresses for the email channel; topic names for the push channel.
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_EMAIL_RECIPIENTS=
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_PUSH_TARGETS=
# Email goes through an SMTP relay reachable without internet access
# (SDD 5.1, local-first). SECURITY is starttls, tls or none.
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_SMTP_HOST=
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_SMTP_PORT=587
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_SMTP_SECURITY=starttls
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_SMTP_USERNAME=
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_SMTP_PASSWORD=
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_SMTP_FROM=
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_SMTP_TIMEOUT_S=10.0
# Push: one JSON POST per message to a self-hosted, ntfy-compatible endpoint.
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_PUSH_URL=
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_PUSH_TOKEN=
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_PUSH_TIMEOUT_S=10.0
# A delivery that failed is retried on later alarm-engine cycles, at most this
# many times and no sooner than this many seconds apart. A failed row is never
# mistaken for a delivered one.
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_RETRY_LIMIT=3
#CHAOS_NOTIFY_RETRY_INTERVAL_S=300

# --- Plugins (SDD 26.2 vendor bindings) -------------------------------------
# "*" loads every plugin found; a comma-separated list loads only those; the
# disabled list always wins, so one line here takes a misbehaving vendor
# integration out of the platform without a rebuild. See docs/plugins.md.
#CHAOS_PLUGINS_ENABLED=*
#CHAOS_PLUGINS_DISABLED=
# A JSON object keyed by plugin name, e.g. {"netbotz": {"host": "10.10.10.40"}}.
# Credentials belong in per-key variables instead, CHAOS_PLUGIN_<NAME>_<KEY>,
# which override the JSON.
#CHAOS_PLUGIN_OPTIONS=
# The mirror engine turns plugin readings into canonical telemetry. It is a
# bus producer, so it does nothing useful while MQTT is disabled.
#CHAOS_PLUGIN_MIRROR_ENABLED=true
